INSERT INTO _s496_b5_m VALUES
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2939,25045,$n$Matthew 25:40 — *Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren.* The sentence to the sheep names the least as his brethren, which tells us whose kin the goats passed by.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2940,25040,$n$Matthew 12:46 — *While he yet talked to the people, behold, his mother and his brethren stood without, desiring to speak with him.* He points to his disciples as his brethren, which shows who the least of these my brethren are.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2941,25045,$n$Matthew 12:46 — *While he yet talked to the people, behold, his mother and his brethren stood without, desiring to speak with him.* His brethren are the family he points out around him, and the goats neglected one of them.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2942,25040,$n$Matthew 28:10 — *go tell my brethren that they go into Galilee.* The risen one calls the frightened disciples his brethren, the same word he uses of the least at the throne.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2943,25045,$n$Matthew 28:10 — *go tell my brethren that they go into Galilee.* After rising he still calls his people brethren, which shows who stood unnoticed before the goats.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2944,25040,$n$John 20:17 — *but go to my brethren, and say unto them, I ascend unto my Father, and your Father.* He gives his brethren the same Father he has, so they are of his household.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2945,25045,$n$John 20:17 — *but go to my brethren, and say unto them, I ascend unto my Father, and your Father.* The brethren share his Father, so refusing the least of them was refusing his own household.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2946,25040,$n$Hebrews 2:11 — *for which cause he is not ashamed to call them brethren.* He is not ashamed to call them brethren, being all of one with them, and so the least are his family.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2947,25045,$n$Hebrews 2:11 — *for which cause he is not ashamed to call them brethren.* He owns the least as his brethren and is all of one with them, so what the goats left undone was left undone for him.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2948,25040,$n$Hebrews 2:16 — *For verily he took not on him the nature of angels; but he took on him the seed of Abraham.* He took on the seed of Abraham, so the brethren are his people by the fathers' blood.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2949,25045,$n$Hebrews 2:16 — *For verily he took not on him the nature of angels; but he took on him the seed of Abraham.* The least are the seed of Abraham whom he took on, so the goats withheld from his own kin.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2950,25040,$n$Romans 8:29 — *For whom he did foreknow, he also did predestinate to be conformed to the image of his Son, that he might be the firstborn among many brethren.* He is the firstborn of many brethren whom the Father foreknew, and those are the ones the sheep served.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2951,25045,$n$Romans 8:29 — *For whom he did foreknow, he also did predestinate to be conformed to the image of his Son, that he might be the firstborn among many brethren.* The firstborn has many foreknown brethren, so neglecting the least of them is neglecting his own.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2952,25040,$n$Deuteronomy 17:15 — *one from among thy brethren shalt thou set king over thee.* The Torah says the one set over the people must come from among his brethren, so he speaks of the least as kin.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2953,25045,$n$Deuteronomy 17:15 — *one from among thy brethren shalt thou set king over thee.* The one set over the people must be a brother, and the goats failed the brethren he is brother to.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2954,25040,$n$Psalm 22:22 — *I will declare thy name unto my brethren: in the midst of the congregation will I praise thee.* He calls the people he declares the Father's name to his brethren, the same word used of the least.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2955,25045,$n$Psalm 22:22 — *I will declare thy name unto my brethren: in the midst of the congregation will I praise thee.* The brethren he names in the congregation are the least the goats passed by.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2956,25040,$n$Proverbs 17:17 — *A friend loveth at all times, and a brother is born for adversity.* A brother is born for adversity, and the sheep acted as brothers to those in it.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2957,25045,$n$Proverbs 17:17 — *A friend loveth at all times, and a brother is born for adversity.* A brother is made for adversity, and the goats stayed away from the adversity of the least.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2958,25040,$n$Acts 9:4 — *And he fell to the earth, and heard a voice saying unto him, Saul, Saul, why persecutest thou me?* Yahusha (Jesus) counts what is done to his people as done to him, as he does at the throne.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2959,25045,$n$Acts 9:4 — *And he fell to the earth, and heard a voice saying unto him, Saul, Saul, why persecutest thou me?* What is done to his people is counted as done to him, whether harm or neglect.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2960,25040,$n$Acts 22:14 — *The Elohim (God) of our fathers hath chosen thee, that thou shouldest know his will.* The Just One who speaks to Paul was sent by the Elohim (God) of the fathers, which places his brethren in their line.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2961,25045,$n$Acts 22:14 — *The Elohim (God) of our fathers hath chosen thee, that thou shouldest know his will.* The Just One is the one the Elohim (God) of the fathers sent, and the goats neglected his people.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2990,25046,$n$Matthew 25:34 — *Then shall the King say unto them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world:* The inheritance was prepared before the world's foundation, and the two ends show who kept it.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2991,25034,$n$Matthew 25:46 — *And these shall go away into everlasting punishment: but the righteous into life eternal.* The end of the sheep, life eternal, is the end of an inheritance prepared from the foundation of the world.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2992,25034,$n$Isaiah 60:1 — *Arise, shine; for thy light is come, and the glory of Yahuah (LORD) is risen upon thee.* The glory of Yahuah (the LORD) rises on Zion, the gathered seed who inherit, and the nations come to that light later.$n$),
('the-day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous-and-the-judgment-of-the-nations-in-wisdom-of-solomon',2993,25046,$n$Isaiah 60:1 — *Arise, shine; for thy light is come, and the glory of Yahuah (LORD) is risen upon thee.* The call to arise and shine fits the sifted seed, with the nations coming afterward to their light.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2994,25034,$n$Isaiah 66:18 — *it shall come, that I will gather all nations and tongues; and they shall come, and see my glory.* The nations are gathered to see his glory, which differs from the sheep's inheritance of the kingdom.$n$),
('the-day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous-and-the-judgment-of-the-nations-in-wisdom-of-solomon',2995,25046,$n$Isaiah 66:18 — *it shall come, that I will gather all nations and tongues; and they shall come, and see my glory.* The nations come to see his glory, apart from the righteous who go into life.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2996,25034,$n$Zechariah 14:16 — *every one that is left of all the nations which came against Jerusalem shall even go up from year to year.* The nations left alive go up yearly to worship, so they are not the sheep who inherit.$n$),
('the-day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous-and-the-judgment-of-the-nations-in-wisdom-of-solomon',2997,25046,$n$Zechariah 14:16 — *every one that is left of all the nations which came against Jerusalem shall even go up from year to year.* The nations left alive keep the feast yearly, and the righteous are the gathered seed over them.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',2998,25034,$n$Revelation 21:24 — *the nations of them which are saved shall walk in the light of it.* The nations walk in the light of the city, which comes after the kingdom the sheep inherit.$n$),
('the-day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous-and-the-judgment-of-the-nations-in-wisdom-of-solomon',2999,25046,$n$Revelation 21:24 — *the nations of them which are saved shall walk in the light of it.* The nations walk in the light of the city, apart from the sifted seed who go into life.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',3000,25034,$n$Revelation 22:1 — *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* The river of life flows from the throne of Elohim (God) and the Lamb, with leaves for the healing of the nations.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',3001,25046,$n$Revelation 22:1 — *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* The life of the righteous is shown as a river and a tree whose leaves heal the nations.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',3002,25034,$n$Revelation 20:4 — *they lived and reigned with Messiah (Christ) a thousand years.* The kingdom the sheep inherit is a reign of a thousand years with Messiah (Christ), on thrones with judgment given.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',3003,25046,$n$Revelation 20:4 — *they lived and reigned with Messiah (Christ) a thousand years.* John shows a reign of a thousand years for those who live, set beside Matthew's life eternal.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',3004,25034,$n$Joel 3:1 — *For, behold, in those days, and in that time, when I shall bring again the captivity of Yahudah (Judah) and Jerusalem,* Joel sets the return of the captives first, and the nations gathered come after, which differs from the sheep's inheritance.$n$),
('the-day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous-and-the-judgment-of-the-nations-in-wisdom-of-solomon',3005,25046,$n$Joel 3:1 — *For, behold, in those days, and in that time, when I shall bring again the captivity of Yahudah (Judah) and Jerusalem,* Joel's return of the captivity stands before the nations are dealt with, and the parting is among the gathered.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',3006,25034,$n$Micah 4:1 — *the mountain of the house of Yahuah (LORD) shall be established in the top of the mountains.* Peoples flow to the mountain of the house of Yahuah (the LORD) in the last days, which is the reign's scene.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',3007,25046,$n$Micah 4:1 — *the mountain of the house of Yahuah (LORD) shall be established in the top of the mountains.* Peoples flow to the mountain in the last days, after the sorting of the gathered.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',3008,25034,$n$Isaiah 2:2 — *the mountain of the LORD’S house shall be established in the top of the mountains.* All nations flow to the mountain of the house of Yahuah (the LORD) in the last days, apart from the sheep's inheritance.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',3009,25046,$n$Isaiah 2:2 — *the mountain of the LORD’S house shall be established in the top of the mountains.* All nations flow to the mountain in the last days, which is later than the sorting of the gathered.$n$),
('parable-of-the-ten-virgins-oil-substance-as-heart-torah-walking-life',4088,25001,$n$Luke 12:35 — *Let your loins be girded about, and your lights burning;* Luke's burning lights are Matthew's lamps, kept by those who wait for the master to return.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4089,25031,$n$Zechariah 14:5 — *Yahuah Elohai (the LORD my God) shall come, and all the saints with thee.* Zechariah has Yahuah (the LORD) come with all his saints, the same company that comes with the Son of Adam.$n$),
('the-judgment-of-the-kings-and-the-mighty-cast-down-in-1-enoch-parables',4090,25031,$n$Deuteronomy 33:2 — *he came with ten thousands of saints: from his right hand went a fiery law for them.* The one who came at Sinai with ten thousands of saints is the one who comes with his holy angels.$n$),
('the-judgment-of-the-kings-and-the-mighty-cast-down-in-1-enoch-parables',4091,25031,$n$2 Thessalonians 1:7 — *And to you who are troubled rest with us, when the Lord Yahusha (Lord Jesus) shall be revealed from heaven with his mighty angels,* He is revealed from heaven with his mighty angels, and the troubled receive rest at that time.$n$),
('the-judgment-of-the-kings-and-the-mighty-cast-down-in-1-enoch-parables',4092,25031,$n$Revelation 19:11 — *he that sat upon him was called Faithful and True, and in righteousness he doth judge and make war.* The one coming from heaven judges in righteousness and is called Faithful and True.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4093,25034,$n$Matthew 12:46 — *While he yet talked to the people, behold, his mother and his brethren stood without, desiring to speak with him.* The blessed of the Father are his family, as when he named his disciples his brethren.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4094,25034,$n$Hebrews 2:11 — *for which cause he is not ashamed to call them brethren.* He is not ashamed to call them brethren, and the inheritance is given to them as his family.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4095,25034,$n$Romans 8:29 — *For whom he did foreknow, he also did predestinate to be conformed to the image of his Son, that he might be the firstborn among many brethren.* Those foreknown are the many brethren of the firstborn, which fits the kingdom prepared before the foundation of the world.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4096,25034,$n$Isaiah 58:6 — *to loose the bands of wickedness, to undo the heavy burdens, and to let the oppressed go free.* Isaiah names the works Yahuah (the LORD) chose, loosing bands and freeing the oppressed, which the throne counts.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4097,25034,$n$Isaiah 61:1 — *to proclaim liberty to the captives, and the opening of the prison to them that are bound.* The anointed one was sent to open the prison to the bound, and the sheep visited those prisoners.$n$),
('the-mercy-toward-the-poor-the-stranger-and-the-needy-as-the-criterion-of-righteousness-in-sirach-and-tobit',4098,25034,$n$Job 31:16 — *If I have withheld the poor from their desire, or have caused the eyes of the widow to fail;* Job measured himself by how he treated the poor and the widow, long before the throne.$n$),
('the-mercy-toward-the-poor-the-stranger-and-the-needy-as-the-criterion-of-righteousness-in-sirach-and-tobit',4099,25034,$n$Proverbs 19:17 — *He that hath pity upon the poor lendeth unto Yahuah (LORD); and that which he hath given will he pay him again.* Mercy to the poor is a loan to Yahuah (the LORD), repaid at the throne.$n$),
('the-mercy-toward-the-poor-the-stranger-and-the-needy-as-the-criterion-of-righteousness-in-sirach-and-tobit',4100,25034,$n$Deuteronomy 10:18 — *He doth execute the judgment of the fatherless and widow, and loveth the stranger, in giving him food and raiment.* The Father loves the stranger by giving food and clothing, the works the sheep are found to have done.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4101,25034,$n$John 20:17 — *but go to my brethren, and say unto them, I ascend unto my Father, and your Father.* The risen one calls the same people his brethren, with the same Father, as at the throne.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4102,25034,$n$Acts 9:4 — *And he fell to the earth, and heard a voice saying unto him, Saul, Saul, why persecutest thou me?* What is done to his people is counted as done to him.$n$),
('the-judgment-of-the-kings-and-the-mighty-cast-down-in-1-enoch-parables',4103,25041,$n$Revelation 20:10 — *the devil that deceived them was cast into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are.* John shows the devil cast into the lake of fire, which Matthew says was prepared for him and his angels.$n$),
('the-judgment-of-the-kings-and-the-mighty-cast-down-in-1-enoch-parables',4104,25041,$n$Revelation 20:14 — *And death and hell were cast into the lake of fire. This is the second death.* The lake of fire is the second death, into which death and hell are cast.$n$),
('the-judgment-of-the-kings-and-the-mighty-cast-down-in-1-enoch-parables',4105,25041,$n$2 Peter 2:4 — *For if Elohim (God) spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell.* The angels that sinned are held for judgment, and the fire was made for them.$n$),
('the-judgment-of-the-kings-and-the-mighty-cast-down-in-1-enoch-parables',4106,25041,$n$Jude 1:6 — *the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation.* Jude names the angels who left their own habitation and are held for judgment, the ones the fire was made for.$n$),
('the-mercy-toward-the-poor-the-stranger-and-the-needy-as-the-criterion-of-righteousness-in-sirach-and-tobit',4107,25041,$n$Proverbs 21:13 — *Whoso stoppeth his ears at the cry of the poor, he also shall cry himself, but shall not be heard.* Whoever shuts his ears to the cry of the poor will cry and not be heard.$n$),
('the-mercy-toward-the-poor-the-stranger-and-the-needy-as-the-criterion-of-righteousness-in-sirach-and-tobit',4108,25041,$n$James 4:17 — *Therefore to him that knoweth to do good, and doeth it not, to him it is sin.* Knowing the good and leaving it undone is sin, which is the charge laid on the goats.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4109,25041,$n$John 3:16 — *For Elohim (God) so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son.* The Father gave his Son, set against the hand that gave nothing, which hears depart from me.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4110,25046,$n$Daniel 12:2 — *some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* Daniel names two ends for those who awake, a life that lasts and a shame that lasts.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4111,25046,$n$Isaiah 66:24 — *their worm shall not die, neither shall their fire be quenched.* Isaiah's worm that does not die and fire not quenched is a lasting end for the transgressors.$n$),
('the-day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous-and-the-judgment-of-the-nations-in-wisdom-of-solomon',4112,25046,$n$Revelation 20:11 — *I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away.* The great white throne is seen after the reign, a later sitting than the throne at his coming.$n$),
('sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations-at-the-throne-of-his-glory',4113,25046,$n$Revelation 21:1 — *And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away; and there was no more sea.* A new heaven and earth appear when the first have passed away, after the sorting.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',3065,26002,$n$Exodus 12:1 — *And Yahuah (LORD) spake unto Moses and Aaron in the land of Egypt, saying,* Yahuah (the LORD) gives Moses and Aaron the passover in Egypt, the feast Yahusha (Jesus) says is two days away.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',3066,26017,$n$Exodus 12:1 — *And Yahuah (LORD) spake unto Moses and Aaron in the land of Egypt, saying,* Yahuah (the LORD) speaks the passover to Moses and Aaron in Egypt, the feast the disciples ask where to prepare.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',3067,26002,$n$John 1:29 — *The next day John seeth Yahusha (Jesus) coming unto him, and saith, Behold the Lamb of Elohim (God), which taketh away the sin of the world.* John the Baptist calls Yahusha (Jesus) the Lamb of Elohim (God), the lamb of the passover he is now two days from.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',3068,26017,$n$John 1:36 — *And looking upon Yahusha (Jesus) as he walked, he saith, Behold the Lamb of Elohim (God)!* John the Baptist points at Yahusha (Jesus) as he walks and calls him the Lamb of Elohim (God).$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',3069,26002,$n$John 19:14 — *And it was the preparation of the passover, and about the sixth hour: and he saith unto the Yahudim (Jews), Behold your King!* John dates the day of the judgment seat as the preparation of the passover, the feast Yahusha (Jesus) named in Matthew.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',3070,26017,$n$John 19:36 — *For these things were done, that the scripture should be fulfilled, A bone of him shall not be broken.* John says not a bone of him is broken, the rule that was laid on the passover lamb in Egypt.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',3071,26002,$n$1 Corinthians 5:7 — *Purge out therefore the old leaven, that ye may be a new lump, as ye are unleavened. For even Messiah (Christ) our passover is sacrificed for us:* Paul names Messiah (Christ) as the passover lamb sacrificed, while still speaking of old leaven purged and unleavened bread kept.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',3072,26017,$n$1 Corinthians 5:7 — *Purge out therefore the old leaven, that ye may be a new lump, as ye are unleavened. For even Messiah (Christ) our passover is sacrificed for us:* Paul says Messiah (Christ) our passover is sacrificed and in the next verse tells them to keep the feast.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',3073,26002,$n$1 Peter 1:18 — *Forasmuch as ye know that ye were not redeemed with corruptible things, as silver and gold, from your vain conversation received by tradition from your fathers;* Peter says redemption was not paid in silver and gold but in the blood of Messiah (Christ), as of a lamb without blemish.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',3074,26017,$n$1 Peter 1:18 — *Forasmuch as ye know that ye were not redeemed with corruptible things, as silver and gold, from your vain conversation received by tradition from your fathers;* Peter says they were redeemed not with silver and gold but with the blood of Messiah (Christ), a lamb without blemish.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',3075,26002,$n$Revelation 5:6 — *stood a Lamb as it had been slain, having seven horns and seven eyes.* John sees a Lamb standing in the midst of the throne as it had been slain, the one Matthew's verse sends to the passover.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',3076,26017,$n$Revelation 5:12 — *Saying with a loud voice, Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing.* Revelation's voices call the Lamb that was slain worthy of power, riches, wisdom, strength, honour, glory and blessing.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',3077,26002,$n$Revelation 7:14 — *have washed their robes, and made them white in the blood of the Lamb.* A great multitude out of great tribulation has washed its robes white in the blood of the Lamb whose death Matthew's verse foretells.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',3078,26017,$n$Revelation 7:14 — *have washed their robes, and made them white in the blood of the Lamb.* Those who came out of great tribulation wash their robes white in the blood of the Lamb, the lamb of the feast now being prepared.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',3079,26002,$n$Revelation 12:11 — *And they overcame him by the blood of the Lamb, and by the word of their testimony; and they loved not their lives unto the death.* Those who overcame the accuser did it by the blood of the Lamb and loved not their lives unto death.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',3080,26017,$n$Revelation 12:11 — *And they overcame him by the blood of the Lamb, and by the word of their testimony; and they loved not their lives unto the death.* The accuser is overcome by the blood of the Lamb and the word of their testimony, by those who loved not their lives.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',3081,26002,$n$Isaiah 53:7 — *yet he opened not his mouth: he is brought as a lamb to the slaughter.* Isaiah's afflicted servant is brought like a lamb to the slaughter and does not open his mouth, the way Yahusha (Jesus) goes to the feast.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',3082,26017,$n$Isaiah 53:7 — *yet he opened not his mouth: he is brought as a lamb to the slaughter.* Isaiah's afflicted servant is brought as a lamb to the slaughter and is silent, as the sheep before her shearers.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',3083,26002,$n$Genesis 22:8 — *And Abraham said, My son, Elohim (God) will provide himself a lamb for a burnt offering: so they went both of them together.* Abraham tells his son that Elohim (God) will provide himself a lamb for a burnt offering, long before the passover lamb of Egypt.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',3084,26017,$n$Genesis 22:8 — *And Abraham said, My son, Elohim (God) will provide himself a lamb for a burnt offering: so they went both of them together.* Abraham says Elohim (God) will provide himself a lamb, the answer the passover meal in Matthew begins to give.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',3085,26002,$n$Revelation 19:7 — *Let us be glad and rejoice, and give honour to him: for the marriage of the Lamb is come, and his wife hath made herself ready.* Revelation ends the lamb's story with the marriage of the Lamb, the same lamb Matthew's verse sends to the passover.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',3086,26017,$n$Revelation 19:7 — *Let us be glad and rejoice, and give honour to him: for the marriage of the Lamb is come, and his wife hath made herself ready.* Revelation's marriage of the Lamb comes at the end of the story whose passover meal Matthew's disciples are preparing.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',4114,26001,$n$Matthew 21:33 — *There was a certain householder, which planted a vineyard, and hedged it round about.* The householder's vineyard let out to husbandmen who beat and kill his servants is the story the council of Matthew 26 is about to live out.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',4115,26001,$n$Matthew 23:34 — *and some of them ye shall kill and crucify.* Yahusha (Jesus) warns the scribes and leaders that some of those he sends they will kill and crucify, the plot he then names in Matthew 26.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',4116,26001,$n$Psalm 2:1 — *Why do the heathen rage, and the people imagine a vain thing?* The psalm asks why the heathen rage and the people imagine a vain thing, and goes on to rulers taking counsel against the anointed.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',4117,26001,$n$John 11:47 — *Then gathered the chief priests and the Pharisees a council, and said, What do we? for this man doeth many miracles.* John shows the chief priests and Pharisees gathering a council over his miracles, the first meeting that leads to the one at Caiaphas's palace.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-plot-and-the-passover-lamb',4118,26001,$n$Exodus 12:1 — *And Yahuah (LORD) spake unto Moses and Aaron in the land of Egypt, saying,* Yahuah (the LORD) speaks to Moses and Aaron in Egypt, the opening of the passover Yahusha (Jesus) names in the next verse.$n$),
('matthew-26-bethany-the-anointing',4119,26006,$n$John 12:1 — *Then Yahusha (Jesus) six days before the passover came to Bethany, where Lazarus was which had been dead, whom he raised from the dead.* John dates the Bethany supper six days before the passover, names Mary as the woman and Judas Iscariot as the one who objects.$n$),
('matthew-26-bethany-the-anointing',4120,26006,$n$Luke 7:36 — *And one of the Pharisees desired him that he would eat with him. And he went into the Pharisee’s house, and sat down to meat.* Luke's woman with an alabaster box comes to a Pharisee's table and weeps at his feet, a separate meal from the one in Bethany.$n$),
('matthew-26-bethany-the-anointing',4121,26006,$n$1 Samuel 10:1 — *hath anointed thee to be captain over his inheritance.* Samuel pours oil on a head to anoint a captain over Yahuah's (the LORD's) inheritance, the act the woman at Bethany repeats.$n$),
('matthew-26-bethany-the-anointing',4122,26006,$n$1 Samuel 16:13 — *anointed him in the midst of his brethren: and the Spirit of Yahuah (LORD) came upon David from that day forward.* Samuel anoints David with the horn of oil in the midst of his brethren, and the Spirit of Yahuah (the LORD) comes upon him.$n$),
('matthew-26-bethany-the-anointing',4123,26006,$n$Psalm 45:7 — *Thou lovest righteousness, and hatest wickedness: therefore Elohim (God), thy Elohim (God), hath anointed thee with the oil of gladness above thy fellows.* The psalm names the king anointed with the oil of gladness above his fellows, the anointing beside the ointment poured at Bethany.$n$),
('matthew-26-bethany-the-anointing',4124,26006,$n$Deuteronomy 15:11 — *the poor shall never cease out of the land: therefore I command thee, saying, Thou shalt open thine hand wide unto thy brother, to thy poor.* Moses says the poor will never cease out of the land and commands the open hand toward them, the words Yahusha (Jesus) draws on.$n$),
('thirty-pieces-of-silver-zekharyah-11-12-13-tanakh-prophetic-fulfillment',4125,26014,$n$John 13:2 — *And supper being ended, the devil having now put into the heart of Judas Iscariot, Simon’s son, to betray him;* John says the devil had put the betrayal into the heart of Judas Iscariot before the supper ended.$n$),
('thirty-pieces-of-silver-zekharyah-11-12-13-tanakh-prophetic-fulfillment',4126,26014,$n$John 13:27 — *And after the sop Satan entered into him. Then said Yahusha (Jesus) unto him, That thou doest, do quickly.* After the sop Satan enters Judas, and Yahusha (Jesus) tells him to do quickly what he does, the table moment behind the thirty pieces.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',4127,26017,$n$Mark 14:12 — *when they killed the passover, his disciples said unto him, Where wilt thou that we go and prepare.* Mark adds that the first day of unleavened bread was when they killed the passover, the day the disciples ask where to prepare it.$n$),
('the-blood-of-the-new-covenant-and-the-faithful-unto-death-for-the-covenant-in-1-and-2-maccabees',4128,26017,$n$Luke 22:7 — *Then came the day of unleavened bread, when the passover must be killed.* Luke says the day of unleavened bread came when the passover must be killed, the same day the disciples ask in Matthew.$n$),
('last-supper-this-is-my-body-this-is-my-blood-of-the-new-testament',4129,26017,$n$1 Corinthians 11:23 — *the same night in which he was betrayed took bread.* Paul says he received from Yahusha (Jesus) what he delivered, that on the night he was betrayed he took bread.$n$),
('last-supper-this-is-my-body-this-is-my-blood-of-the-new-testament',4130,26017,$n$Exodus 24:8 — *Behold the blood of the covenant, which Yahuah (LORD) hath made with you concerning all these words.* Moses sprinkles the blood on the people and says it is the blood of the covenant Yahuah (the LORD) made concerning all these words.$n$),
('last-supper-this-is-my-body-this-is-my-blood-of-the-new-testament',4131,26017,$n$Jeremiah 31:31 — *Behold, the days come, saith Yahuah (LORD), that I will make a new covenant with the house of Yashar'el (Israel), and with the house of Yahudah (Judah):* Yahuah (the LORD) promises a new covenant with the house of Yashar'el (Israel) and the house of Yahudah (Judah).$n$),
('last-supper-this-is-my-body-this-is-my-blood-of-the-new-testament',4132,26017,$n$Isaiah 53:10 — *when thou shalt make his soul an offering for sin, he shall see his seed.* Isaiah says the servant makes his soul an offering for sin and shall see his seed, the many of the cup.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-arrest',4133,26047,$n$Mark 14:43 — *cometh Judas, one of the twelve, and with him a great multitude with swords and staves, from the chief priests and the scribes and the elders.* Mark has Judas arrive with a great multitude with swords and staves sent from the chief priests, the scribes and the elders.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-arrest',4134,26047,$n$Luke 22:47 — *he that was called Judas, one of the twelve, went before them, and drew near unto Yahusha (Jesus) to kiss him.* Luke has Judas go before the multitude to kiss him, and adds the question put to Judas and the healing of the ear.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-arrest',4135,26047,$n$John 18:2 — *And Judas also, which betrayed him, knew the place: for Yahusha (Jesus) ofttimes resorted thither with his disciples.* John says Judas knew the garden because Yahusha (Jesus) often went there with his disciples.$n$),
('the-betrayer-the-double-tongue-and-the-watch-against-temptation-in-sirach',4136,26047,$n$Proverbs 27:6 — *Faithful are the wounds of a friend; but the kisses of an enemy are deceitful.* Proverbs says a friend's wounds are faithful and an enemy's kisses are deceitful, the kind of kiss Judas gives.$n$),
('the-betrayer-the-double-tongue-and-the-watch-against-temptation-in-sirach',4137,26047,$n$Psalm 55:12 — *For it was not an enemy that reproached me; then I could have borne it.* The psalmist says it was no enemy but his own equal and acquaintance who reproached him, the grief of Judas's coming.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-arrest',4138,26047,$n$Genesis 9:6 — *Whoso sheddeth man’s blood, by man shall his blood be shed: for in the image of Elohim (God) made he man.* Genesis gives the measure that whoever sheds man's blood has his own shed, the rule behind the word about the sword.$n$),
('the-shepherd-smitten-and-the-temple-veil-rent-in-the-testaments-of-the-twelve',4139,26047,$n$Zechariah 13:7 — *smite the shepherd, and the sheep shall be scattered: and I will turn mine hand upon the little ones.* Yahuah (the LORD) bids the sword smite the shepherd and scatter the sheep, the verse Matthew quotes at 26:31.$n$),
('matthew-26-the-arrest',4140,26047,$n$John 10:17 — *Therefore doth my Father love me, because I lay down my life, that I might take it again.* John says the Father loves him because he lays down his life, which no man takes from him.$n$),
('the-elect-one-vindicated-on-the-throne-and-the-kings-condemned-in-1-enoch-46-48-62-63',4141,26057,$n$Mark 14:53 — *and with him were assembled all the chief priests and the elders and the scribes.* Mark adds that all the chief priests, the elders and the scribes were assembled with the high priest.$n$),
('the-elect-one-vindicated-on-the-throne-and-the-kings-condemned-in-1-enoch-46-48-62-63',4142,26057,$n$Luke 22:54 — *Then took they him, and led him, and brought him into the high priest’s house. And Peter followed afar off.* Luke brings Yahusha (Jesus) into the high priest's house with Peter following afar off.$n$),
('the-elect-one-vindicated-on-the-throne-and-the-kings-condemned-in-1-enoch-46-48-62-63',4143,26057,$n$Luke 22:63 — *And the men that held Yahusha (Jesus) mocked him, and smote him.* Luke says the men holding Yahusha (Jesus) mocked and struck him, in his own order of events.$n$),
('the-elect-one-vindicated-on-the-throne-and-the-kings-condemned-in-1-enoch-46-48-62-63',4144,26057,$n$John 18:13 — *And led him away to Annas first; for he was father in law to Caiaphas, which was the high priest that same year.* John says they led him to Annas first, father in law to Caiaphas, the high priest that year.$n$),
('the-elect-one-vindicated-on-the-throne-and-the-kings-condemned-in-1-enoch-46-48-62-63',4145,26057,$n$John 18:19 — *The high priest then asked Yahusha (Jesus) of his disciples, and of his doctrine.* John records the high priest asking Yahusha (Jesus) about his disciples and his doctrine.$n$),
('sanhedrin-trial-tehillim-110-and-daniel-7-self-identification-at-the-kings-own-mouth',4146,26057,$n$Psalm 110:1 — *Yahuah (LORD) said unto my Lord, Sit thou at my right hand, until I make thine enemies thy footstool.* Yahuah (the LORD) tells the one David addresses to sit at his right hand, the seat Yahusha (Jesus) claims before the council.$n$),
('sanhedrin-trial-tehillim-110-and-daniel-7-self-identification-at-the-kings-own-mouth',4147,26057,$n$Daniel 7:13 — *one like the Son of Adam came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days.* Daniel sees one like the Son of Adam come with the clouds of heaven to the Ancient of days, the verse Yahusha (Jesus) draws on.$n$),
('the-elect-one-vindicated-on-the-throne-and-the-kings-condemned-in-1-enoch-46-48-62-63',4148,26057,$n$Isaiah 53:7 — *yet he opened not his mouth: he is brought as a lamb to the slaughter.* Isaiah's afflicted servant opens not his mouth, the silence Yahusha (Jesus) keeps before the high priest.$n$),
('the-elect-one-vindicated-on-the-throne-and-the-kings-condemned-in-1-enoch-46-48-62-63',4149,26057,$n$Isaiah 50:6 — *I gave my back to the smiters, and my cheeks to them that plucked off the hair: I hid not my face from shame and spitting.* Isaiah's servant gives his back to the smiters and hides not his face from shame and spitting.$n$),
('the-elect-one-vindicated-on-the-throne-and-the-kings-condemned-in-1-enoch-46-48-62-63',4150,26057,$n$Deuteronomy 19:15 — *at the mouth of two witnesses, or at the mouth of three witnesses, shall the matter be established.* The Torah requires two or three witnesses before a matter is established, a rule the council could not meet.$n$),
('matthew-26-peters-denial',4151,26069,$n$Mark 14:66 — *And as Peter was beneath in the palace, there cometh one of the maids of the high priest:* Mark places Peter beneath in the palace, where one of the high priest's maids comes to him.$n$),
('matthew-26-peters-denial',4152,26069,$n$Luke 22:54 — *Then took they him, and led him, and brought him into the high priest’s house. And Peter followed afar off.* Luke puts Peter in the high priest's house, following afar off, before the look Yahusha (Jesus) gives him.$n$),
('matthew-26-peters-denial',4153,26069,$n$John 18:15 — *that disciple was known unto the high priest, and went in with Yahusha (Jesus) into the palace of the high priest.* John says another disciple known to the high priest went in with Yahusha (Jesus) and later brought Peter in.$n$),
('matthew-26-peters-denial',4154,26069,$n$John 18:25 — *Art not thou also one of his disciples? He denied it, and said, I am not.* John has Peter warming himself at the fire, asked if he is a disciple, and denying it.$n$),
('matthew-26-peters-denial',4155,26069,$n$Matthew 26:33 — *Peter answered and said unto him, Though all men shall be offended because of thee, yet will I never be offended.* Peter's promise that he would never be offended is the saying his three denials answer in the same chapter.$n$),
('matthew-26-peters-denial',4156,26069,$n$John 21:15 — *lovest thou me more than these? He saith unto him, Yea, Adonai (Lord); thou knowest that I love thee. He saith unto him, Feed my lambs.* Yahusha (Jesus) asks Peter if he loves him and gives him lambs to feed, the restoration after the denial.$n$),
('matthew-26-peters-denial',4157,26069,$n$Psalm 51:17 — *The sacrifices of Elohim (God) are a broken spirit: a broken and a contrite heart, O Elohim (God), thou wilt not despise.* David says the sacrifice Elohim (God) wants is a broken spirit and a contrite heart he will not despise.$n$),
('matthew-26-peters-denial',4158,26069,$n$Joel 2:12 — *Therefore also now, saith Yahuah (LORD), turn ye even to me with all your heart, and with fasting, and with weeping, and with mourning:* Yahuah (the LORD) calls through Joel for a turn with all the heart, with weeping, the turning Peter makes.$n$),
('matthew-27-judas-and-the-potters-field',4159,27001,$n$Zechariah 11:12 — *So they weighed for my price thirty pieces of silver.* The shepherd is paid thirty pieces of silver for his work, the sum later weighed out as the price on Yahusha (Jesus).$n$),
('matthew-27-judas-and-the-potters-field',4160,27001,$n$Jeremiah 19:1 — *Thus saith Yahuah (LORD), Go and get a potter’s earthen bottle, and take of the ancients of the people, and of the ancients of the priests;* Jeremiah takes a potter's bottle to the elders and priests in the valley of Hinnom, where the charge is innocent blood.$n$),
('matthew-27-judas-and-the-potters-field',4161,27001,$n$Jeremiah 32:6 — *And Jeremiah said, The word of Yahuah (LORD) came unto me, saying,* Jeremiah buys a field at the word of Yahuah (the LORD) and weighs out silver for it, the other field behind the potter's field.$n$),
('matthew-27-judas-and-the-potters-field',4162,27001,$n$Psalm 109:8 — *Let his days be few; and let another take his office.* David asks that another take the office of the man who turns on him, the verse Peter later reads over Judas.$n$),
('matthew-27-judas-and-the-potters-field',4163,27001,$n$Acts 1:16 — *which the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit) by the mouth of David spake before concerning Judas.* Peter tells the disciples that David spoke by the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit) about Judas, who guided those who took Yahusha (Jesus).$n$),
('matthew-27-judas-and-the-potters-field',4164,27001,$n$Deuteronomy 23:18 — *Thou shalt not bring the hire of a whore, or the price of a dog, into the house of Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God).* The Torah keeps the hire of a whore and the price of a dog out of the house of Yahuah (the LORD), the line the priests lean on.$n$),
('matthew-27-pilate-and-barabbas',4165,27011,$n$Mark 15:1 — *the chief priests held a consultation with the elders and scribes and the whole council.* Mark has the whole council bind Yahusha (Jesus) in the morning and hand him to Pilate.$n$),
('matthew-27-pilate-and-barabbas',4166,27011,$n$Luke 23:1 — *And the whole multitude of them arose, and led him unto Pilate.* Luke has the whole company lead Yahusha (Jesus) to Pilate and gives the charge that stands behind the governor's question.$n$),
('matthew-27-pilate-and-barabbas',4167,27011,$n$John 18:28 — *they themselves went not into the judgment hall, lest they should be defiled; but that they might eat the passover.* The rulers who bring Yahusha (Jesus) to Pilate will not enter his hall, lest they be defiled before they eat the passover.$n$),
('matthew-27-pilate-and-barabbas',4168,27011,$n$Isaiah 53:7 — *he is brought as a lamb to the slaughter, and as a sheep before her shearers is dumb.* Isaiah's servant is afflicted and silent as a lamb before the slaughter, the silence Pilate marvels at.$n$),
('his-blood-be-on-us-and-on-our-children-system-not-people-and-the-yom-kippur-blood-substance',4169,27011,$n$Deuteronomy 21:1 — *and it be not known who hath slain him.* Deuteronomy 21 gives the elders' cleansing for a killing no one can name, the ceremony Pilate's hand-washing borrows.$n$),
('matthew-27-pilate-and-barabbas',4170,27011,$n$Acts 3:13 — *hath glorified his Son Yahusha (Jesus); whom ye delivered up, and denied him in the presence of Pilate, when he was determined to let him go.* Peter says the Elohim (God) of the fathers glorified Yahusha (Jesus), and that Pilate was determined to release him.$n$),
('his-blood-be-on-us-and-on-our-children-system-not-people-and-the-yom-kippur-blood-substance',4171,27011,$n$Acts 4:25 — *Who by the mouth of thy servant David hast said, Why did the heathen rage, and the people imagine vain things?* The believers pray David's psalm about the rulers raging against the anointed, naming the gathering that stood before Pilate.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4172,27027,$n$Mark 15:16 — *And the soldiers led him away into the hall, called Prætorium; and they call together the whole band.* Mark names the hall as the Prætorium and has the soldiers call together the whole band.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4173,27027,$n$Luke 23:26 — *they laid hold upon one Simon, a Cyrenian, coming out of the country, and on him they laid the cross.* Luke names Simon the Cyrenian as the man made to carry the cross after Yahusha (Jesus).$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4174,27027,$n$John 19:17 — *And he bearing his cross went forth into a place called the place of a skull, which is called in the Hebrew Golgotha:* John has Yahusha (Jesus) go out bearing his cross to Golgotha, the place of a skull.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4175,27027,$n$Isaiah 50:6 — *I hid not my face from shame and spitting.* The servant gives his back to the smiters and does not hide his face from shame and spitting.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4176,27027,$n$Isaiah 53:3 — *He is despised and rejected of men; a man of sorrows, and acquainted with grief.* The servant is despised and rejected, a man of sorrows whom men would not look at.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4177,27027,$n$Isaiah 53:7 — *He was oppressed, and he was afflicted, yet he opened not his mouth.* The servant is oppressed and afflicted and opens not his mouth, the silence held through the soldiers' sport.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4178,27027,$n$Psalm 22:7 — *All they that see me laugh me to scorn: they shoot out the lip, they shake the head, saying,* David's psalm has the onlookers laugh him to scorn and shake the head, as the crowd does at the cross.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4179,27027,$n$Psalm 22:16 — *For dogs have compassed me: the assembly of the wicked have inclosed me: they pierced my hands and my feet.* The psalmist is ringed by dogs and an assembly of the wicked, and his hands and feet are pierced.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4180,27027,$n$Genesis 3:15 — *between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.* The woman's seed will bruise the serpent's head while the serpent bruises his heel, read here beside the soldiers' sport.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4181,27027,$n$Genesis 3:18 — *Thorns also and thistles shall it bring forth to thee; and thou shalt eat the herb of the field;* The ground under the curse brings forth thorns and thistles, read beside the crown of thorns.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4182,27039,$n$Mark 15:29 — *And they that passed by railed on him, wagging their heads, and saying, Ah, thou that destroyest the temple, and buildest it in three days,* Mark has the passers-by cry Ah and throw the temple saying at him as they wag their heads.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4183,27039,$n$Luke 23:35 — *And the people stood beholding. And the rulers also with them derided him, saying, He saved others; let him save himself, if he be Messiah (Christ), the chosen of Elohim (God).* Luke names the rulers among the onlookers, deriding him as one who saved others and cannot save himself.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4184,27039,$n$John 19:25 — *Now there stood by the cross of Yahusha (Jesus) his mother, and his mother’s sister, Mary the wife of Cleophas, and Mary Magdalene.* John names the women standing by the cross, among them his mother and Mary Magdalene.$n$),
('eli-eli-lama-sabachthani-the-tehillim-22-citation-and-the-tehillim-22-as-a-whole-substance',4185,27039,$n$Psalm 22:1 — *why hast thou forsaken me? why art thou so far from helping me, and from the words of my roaring?* David's opening cry, the line Yahusha (Jesus) takes up, which begins a psalm and does not close it.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4186,27039,$n$Psalm 69:21 — *They gave me also gall for my meat; and in my thirst they gave me vinegar to drink.* David's gall for meat and vinegar for thirst, the cup the crowd offers him at the cross.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4187,27039,$n$Amos 8:9 — *that I will cause the sun to go down at noon, and I will darken the earth in the clear day.* Amos has the sun go down at noon in that day, the darkness over the land at the cross.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4188,27039,$n$John 10:17 — *Therefore doth my Father love me, because I lay down my life, that I might take it again.* He says his Father loves him because he lays down his life to take it again, not as a man overpowered.$n$),
('substantial-crucifixion-tanakh-substances-tehillim-22-and-yeshayahu-53-and-zekharyah-12-10',4189,27039,$n$Hebrews 5:7 — *when he had offered up prayers and supplications with strong crying and tears unto him that was able to save him from death.* Hebrews says in the days of his flesh he prayed with strong crying and tears to the one able to save him.$n$),
('veil-of-the-temple-rent-and-the-substantial-access-to-the-father-through-the-cross',4190,27051,$n$John 19:31 — *because it was the preparation, that the bodies should not remain upon the cross on the sabbath day, (for that sabbath day was an high day,).* John places the tearing of the veil in the afternoon of the preparation, with a high-day Sabbath close at hand.$n$),
('matthew-27-the-burial',4191,27057,$n$Mark 15:42 — *And now when the even was come, because it was the preparation, that is, the day before the sabbath,* Mark says it was the evening of the preparation, the day before the Sabbath, when Joseph came for the body.$n$),
('matthew-27-the-burial',4192,27057,$n$Luke 23:50 — *And, behold, there was a man named Joseph, a counsellor; and he was a good man, and a just:* Luke calls Joseph a counsellor, a good man and a just, who had not consented to the council's deed.$n$),
('matthew-27-the-burial',4193,27057,$n$John 19:38 — *Joseph of Arimathaea, being a disciple of Yahusha (Jesus), but secretly for fear of the Yahudim (Jews), besought Pilate.* John says Joseph was a disciple in secret and asked Pilate for the body, which Pilate gave him.$n$),
('matthew-27-the-burial',4194,27057,$n$Isaiah 53:9 — *and with the rich in his death; because he had done no violence, neither was any deceit in his mouth.* Isaiah says the servant's grave was with the rich in his death, because he had done no violence.$n$),
('matthew-27-the-burial',4195,27057,$n$Matthew 28:11 — *Now when they were going, behold, some of the watch came into the city, and shewed unto the chief priests all the things that were done.* Some of the watch come into the city and tell the chief priests all that was done at the tomb.$n$),
('the-resurrection-substance-tehillim-16-and-tehillim-22-vindication-substance',4196,28001,$n$Matthew 12:38 — *Then certain of the scribes and of the Pharisees answered, saying, Master, we would see a sign from thee.* The scribes and Pharisees ask for a sign, and the only one Yahusha (Jesus) gives them is Jonah's, the one the sepulchre answers.$n$),
('the-resurrection-substance-tehillim-16-and-tehillim-22-vindication-substance',4197,28001,$n$Matthew 26:32 — *But after I am risen again, I will go before you into Galilee.* Before his arrest Yahusha (Jesus) says he will go before his disciples into Galilee after he is raised, and the angel at the tomb repeats it.$n$),
('women-as-the-first-witnesses-of-the-resurrection-and-the-faithful-witness-substance',4198,28001,$n$John 20:17 — *go to my brethren, and say unto them, I ascend unto my Father, and your Father.* Mary is sent to his brethren with word that he ascends to his Father and theirs, the same errand the women in Matthew are given.$n$),
('the-king-ascending-and-the-tribes-rising-each-over-his-tribe-in-testaments-of-the-twelve',4199,28001,$n$Matthew 25:40 — *Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.* Yahusha (Jesus) counts what is done to the least of his brethren as done to him, the same brethren the risen one sends the women to.$n$),
('the-king-ascending-and-the-tribes-rising-each-over-his-tribe-in-testaments-of-the-twelve',4200,28001,$n$Hebrews 2:11 — *For both he that sanctifieth and they who are sanctified are all of one: for which cause he is not ashamed to call them brethren,* The one who sanctifies and those sanctified are all of one, which is why he is not ashamed to call them brethren.$n$),
('the-resurrection-substance-tehillim-16-and-tehillim-22-vindication-substance',4201,28001,$n$Leviticus 23:15 — *from the morrow after the sabbath, from the day that ye brought the sheaf of the wave offering.* The count to the feast of weeks starts the morrow after the sabbath, the same kind of morning on which the women find the tomb empty.$n$),
('matthew-28-the-watch-and-the-story-they-paid-for',4202,28011,$n$Matthew 27:62 — *Now the next day, that followed the day of the preparation, the chief priests and Pharisees came together unto Pilate,* The chief priests and Pharisees go to Pilate to have the sepulchre made sure, the guard that later brings them the truth.$n$),
('matthew-28-the-watch-and-the-story-they-paid-for',4203,28011,$n$Acts 4:1 — *And as they spake unto the people, the priests, and the captain of the temple, and the Sadducees, came upon them,* The priests, the captain of the temple and the Sadducees come upon the disciples for preaching the resurrection, the same office that bought the guard's story.$n$),
('matthew-28-the-watch-and-the-story-they-paid-for',4204,28011,$n$Acts 5:17 — *Then the high priest rose up, and all they that were with him, (which is the sect of the Sadducees,) and were filled with indignation,* The high priest and the Sadducees rise up in indignation against the apostles, the same circle that answered the empty tomb with a paid story.$n$),
('the-king-ascending-and-the-tribes-rising-each-over-his-tribe-in-testaments-of-the-twelve',4205,28016,$n$Matthew 26:32 — *But after I am risen again, I will go before you into Galilee.* Yahusha (Jesus) promises on the night of his arrest to go before his disciples into Galilee, and the eleven go where he said.$n$),
('the-king-ascending-and-the-tribes-rising-each-over-his-tribe-in-testaments-of-the-twelve',4206,28016,$n$Matthew 17:1 — *And after six days Yahusha (Jesus) taketh Peter, James, and John his brother, and bringeth them up into an high mountain apart,* The mountain of the transfiguration is another mountain than the one in Galilee; what they share is that he chooses the place and the ones who come.$n$),
('the-king-ascending-and-the-tribes-rising-each-over-his-tribe-in-testaments-of-the-twelve',4207,28016,$n$Matthew 5:1 — *And seeing the multitudes, he went up into a mountain: and when he was set, his disciples came unto him:* On the mountain of the Sermon he sits and teaches his disciples; the teaching they are later sent to carry on began there.$n$),
('the-king-resurrected-and-ascended-sending-out-the-twelve-witnessed-in-ascension-of-isaiah-11',4208,28016,$n$Luke 24:36 — *And as they thus spake, Yahusha (Jesus) himself stood in the midst of them, and saith unto them, Peace be unto you.* Yahusha (Jesus) stands in the midst of the disciples with peace, and answers their fear that he is a spirit by letting them handle him.$n$),
('the-king-resurrected-and-ascended-sending-out-the-twelve-witnessed-in-ascension-of-isaiah-11',4209,28016,$n$John 20:24 — *But Thomas, one of the twelve, called Didymus, was not with them when Yahusha (Jesus) came.* Thomas is absent when Yahusha (Jesus) first comes, and his refusal to believe without seeing is the doubt Matthew mentions only briefly.$n$),
('the-king-resurrected-and-ascended-sending-out-the-twelve-witnessed-in-ascension-of-isaiah-11',4210,28016,$n$Acts 1:15 — *And in those days Peter stood up in the midst of the disciples, and said, (the number of names together were about an hundred and twenty,)* Peter stands among about a hundred and twenty disciples to speak of the place left by Judas, which restores the number of the twelve.$n$),
('great-commission-all-nations-as-territories-of-the-scattered-seed-not-categorical-three-categories-substance',4211,28018,$n$Mark 16:14 — *upbraided them with their unbelief and hardness of heart, because they believed not them which had seen him after he was risen.* Mark has the risen one rebuke the eleven for unbelief at table and then send them into all the world.$n$),
('great-commission-all-nations-as-territories-of-the-scattered-seed-not-categorical-three-categories-substance',4212,28018,$n$Luke 24:44 — *that all things must be fulfilled, which were written in the law of Moses, and in the prophets, and in the psalms, concerning me.* Luke has Yahusha (Jesus) point the disciples to the law, the prophets and the psalms before he sends them to preach among all nations.$n$),
('great-commission-all-nations-as-territories-of-the-scattered-seed-not-categorical-three-categories-substance',4213,28018,$n$John 20:21 — *Then said Yahusha (Jesus) to them again, Peace be unto you: as my Father hath sent me, even so send I you.* Yahusha (Jesus) sends the disciples as the Father sent him, which is the Father's errand passing through the Son.$n$),
('all-power-given-the-son-of-adam-enthroned-on-the-throne-of-glory-in-1-enoch-parables',4214,28018,$n$Psalm 110:1 — *Yahuah (LORD) said unto my Lord, Sit thou at my right hand, until I make thine enemies thy footstool.* Yahuah (the LORD) seats the one David addresses at his right hand until his enemies are a footstool, the giving Matthew's words describe.$n$),
('all-power-given-the-son-of-adam-enthroned-on-the-throne-of-glory-in-1-enoch-parables',4215,28018,$n$Psalm 8:6 — *Thou madest him to have dominion over the works of thy hands; thou hast put all things under his feet:* The son of Adam has all things put under his feet by Yahuah (the LORD), the dominion Matthew's risen Yahusha (Jesus) says is given him.$n$),
('trinitarian-baptism-formula-and-the-name-of-yahusha-in-the-formless-formed-grid',4216,28018,$n$Matthew 1:21 — *And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name Yahusha (JESUS): for he shall save his people from their sins.* The angel names the child Yahusha (Jesus), who will save his people from their sins, the name that is with them to the end of the book.$n$),
('trinitarian-baptism-formula-and-the-name-of-yahusha-in-the-formless-formed-grid',4217,28018,$n$Matthew 1:23 — *Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, and they shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, Elohim (God) with us.* Immanuel, Elohim (God) with us, opens the book as the promise that Yahusha (Jesus) closes with I am with you alway.$n$),
('teaching-them-to-observe-all-things-i-have-commanded-you-heart-torah-closing-the-anti-antinomian-bookend',4218,28018,$n$Matthew 5:17 — *Think not that I am come to destroy the law, or the prophets: I am not come to destroy, but to fulfil.* He says he did not come to destroy the law or the prophets, and the closing charge to teach all he commanded keeps that standing.$n$),
('teaching-them-to-observe-all-things-i-have-commanded-you-heart-torah-closing-the-anti-antinomian-bookend',4219,28018,$n$Matthew 7:21 — *but he that doeth the will of my Father which is in heaven.* Entering the kingdom depends on doing the Father's will, which is what the eleven are sent to teach at the end of Matthew.$n$),
('teaching-them-to-observe-all-things-i-have-commanded-you-heart-torah-closing-the-anti-antinomian-bookend',4220,28018,$n$John 14:15 — *If ye love me, keep my commandments.* Love for Yahusha (Jesus) is shown by keeping his commandments, the same commandments the eleven are sent to teach.$n$);
